Lunara loved a sailor named Derin, who sang songs that reached even the darkest trenches. Unlike Selara's doomed love, Lunara made a different choice. She asked the Ocean Keeper for help. "Grant him the gift of water-breath," she pleaded, "so he may live in both worlds."

The Ocean Keeper agreed, but with a price: "He may breathe beneath the waves, but he will forget his human life—his name, his past, his very self."

